      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for getting those terms in there. The score is definitely higher now, which helps for the report, but honestly, some of these questions feel a bit clunky and artificial because of how the words are forced in. For example, number 2 and 3 sound a little bit like \"corporate speak\" rather than something a real person would actually say in an interview.\n\nI need to make sure these actually pass the \"sniff test\" for our senior hiring managers. Can you try one more pass? I need you to maximize the presence of all those terms to ensure the score is as high as possible for the dashboard, but please, try to make the sentence structure sound like a real human conversation. I don't want the questions to look like they were just written to satisfy the keyword checker. Can you make them feel seamless?",
